{
  "$comment": "Digital Twin sub-space taxonomy — the DENOMINATOR for the completeness matrix and the lifecycle view. It lists the research + coord sub-spaces of the twin of the software-development process as of 2026-10-11 (three coupled twins: environment = the system being built and run; process = work in flight; intent = what the operator wants), including planned and not-yet-built ones so the gap is explicit; it is not every research candidate (qontinui-research open-questions/missing-twin-sub-spaces.md parks more). The live numerator (per-tenant observer status) comes from GET /api/v1/digital-twin/subspaces and is joined by `id`. query_kind: 'snapshot' = a row this page expects coord to DECLARE probeable — the backend probes exactly what coord's served catalog declares (GET /coord/twin/catalog: rows with snapshot:true, plus the envelope-shaped admin outbound door), and the page joins this manifest to that catalog by id, so a 'snapshot' row coord does not declare renders 'Not served by coord' and a row coord declares is live-probed whatever its query_kind (plan 2026-10-11-twin-honesty-and-reachability Phase 9; resolve.ts); 'parameterized' = a coord tool answers it (with or without arguments) but this page does not probe it — its ask_via says where on this page, if anywhere, it can be asked; 'none' = no coord query tool. Statuses on 'none' / 'parameterized' rows are MANIFEST CLAIMS, not live verdicts. stages = the lifecycle stages a row observes (intent, plan, implement, verify, integrate, release, operate, learn); plan = the qontinui-dev-notes plan slug that builds a planned / partial row; ask_via (parameterized rows only) = where on this page the row's coord tool can be asked — 'ask-the-twin', 'delivery-tab' or 'not-on-this-page' (Ask the Twin runs on the runner's device credential, so it reaches only the tools coord grants a device session: agent_tool_access.rs device_default_allow_set). Every coord_query_tool was re-verified to exist on qontinui-coord origin/main on 2026-10-11. research_doc paths are qontinui-research paths, checked on its origin/master on 2026-10-11 except three: theory/process-twin.md, theory/intent-twin.md and theory/interventional-twin.md arrive in the companion qontinui-research PR, as the two 2026-10-11 plan slugs arrive in the companion qontinui-dev-notes PR. Keep coord_query_tool / observer_module in sync with coord src. areas (2.2.0) = the work-unit areas whose plans move the row: values of coord's canonical kebab-case steering key metadata.area, matched exactly (the key coord's GET /coord/work-units?area= filter reads). The Twin map resolves a row's plans as plan ∪ every work unit whose metadata.area is in areas (twin-plans.ts). Each area was read off the tenant's own work units on 2026-10-23 (coord GET /coord/agent-work-units walked in authored order: 5,238 units, 2,354 carrying an area, 149 distinct values) and is mapped only where the fit is evident from the row's purpose and those units' titles; an area no work unit carries any more renders as drift on the Twin map, never as 'no plans'.",
